flowchart TD
    Node["Superstep N<br/>node returns a partial update"] --> Reducer["Reducer folds that update<br/>into the channel's value"]
    Reducer --> Strategy{"How is the channel persisted?"}

    Strategy -->|"Full snapshot<br/>(the default)"| Put["Re-serialize the WHOLE<br/>channel value, every step"]
    Strategy -->|"Incremental<br/>(delta + periodic snapshot)"| Delta["Serialize only this step's<br/>update, into a writes table"]

    Put --> PutCost["O(state) per step<br/>O(n squared) per run<br/>1.34 MB over 100 steps"]

    Delta --> Snap{"steps since snapshot<br/>>= snapshot_frequency?"}
    Snap -->|Yes| Full["Write a full snapshot,<br/>bounding future replay depth"]
    Snap -->|No| Sentinel["Checkpoint holds a sentinel;<br/>real state lives in the writes table"]
    Full --> DeltaCost["O(1) per step<br/>O(n) per run<br/>60 KB over 100 steps"]
    Sentinel --> DeltaCost

    PutCost --> Read["Resume: read state back"]
    DeltaCost --> Read

    Read --> Which{"What has to be read?"}
    Which -->|"Snapshot"| Deser["Deserialize one value.<br/>Replay depth: zero."]
    Which -->|"Incremental"| Replay["Deserialize the nearest snapshot,<br/>then replay every ancestor write<br/>through the reducer"]

    Replay --> Invariant["Replay batches those writes differently<br/>than execution produced them.<br/>A reducer that is not batching-invariant<br/>reconstructs DIFFERENT state, silently."]

    Deser --> Owner["Write cost is paid by the service doing the work.<br/>Read cost is paid by whoever is waiting on resume —<br/>often a user, on the recovery path."]
    Invariant --> Owner
